Z||000007||thomas_l||11-30-2001||08:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>Try buying a washer or dryer from Sears.  You find out you must also buy a power cord for $5.  What a joke.  You [b]have</B> to have it, so why don't they just include it in the purchase?  *Sheesh*   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I know it's not the same as your camera order, but sort of a similar principle.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Probably because there are about 5 different service sockets for 220V (dryer). At least they could give you a voucher for one tho  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||thomas_l||11-30-2001||08:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Wait till you buy a DVD player and have it break in 3 weeks, and find out that you have voided the warranty because you brought it into canada.. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually - you are on to something there. I saw a news article somewhere about the big discount electronics shops you see, especially on the net. They found that in many cases the articles being sold so cheap were actually made for sale in another country. The story got started by some guy getting a smoking good deal on a camcorder. When it arrived there were the bare minimum accessories and instructions and controls were Japanese. Oh yeah - since it was PAL and not NTSC, it was not useable on any North American video equipment.<P>You Get What You Pay For.||||reg||3
Z||000009||Cliff Pennock||11-30-2001||10:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by thomas_l:<BR><B>They found that in many cases the articles being sold so cheap were actually made for sale in another country.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I <B>am</B> in another country.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Prices here in Europe are rediculously high for luxury goods. In fact, if the camera would break the price difference would buy me a plane-ticket so I could bring it in personally!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||thomas_l||11-30-2001||11:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B> Well, I am in another country.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You got me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'm sure they'll provide the Dutch version for a small extra charge  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
