Z||000013||Patrick's Dad||12-01-2001||11:45 AM||||&lt;quote&gt;Prices here in Europe are rediculously high for luxury goods.&lt;/quote&gt;<P>Cliff, this is because of VAT.<P>Interestingly, I used to have a number of Scandinavian and German customers who came to visit the US subsidiary of the business, then come buy stuff from me, while I've seen European versions of the same equipment for sale in Jamaica (Honeymoon), as well as here in the US, for below US cost. Wierd.<P>Actually, if I travelled there, I think that I would get a better deal, as VAT would be refunded to me as I left the country. Of course, no USA warranty.<P>Check with B&H, (http://bhphoto.com) as you can get gray (No warranty issues for you, anyway), and they're mostly reputable.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cliff Pennock||12-01-2001||01:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Patrick's Dad:<BR><B>Cliff, this is because of VAT.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>VAT (sales tax) is very high here (19%), but even without that prices for luxury goods here are about 1.5x-2x as high as in the states.<P>Price including sales tax for the Coolpix 996 is $1100 here.<BR>||||reg||1
